r($,"bA3","rH",()=>{var q="If you got high during the scene gain Fortune, otherwise gain Misfortune. Your addiction must cost 1 supply to use. In Combat it requires the use of your Action or Reaction to get high. You remain high for the remainder of the situation. Pick 1 skill, and gain disadvantage on all checks with it while high. Pick one of the below mods for your addiction.\n\nQuick: During Combat, Use an Item interaction instead of a reaction or action. Adventuring, When you roll the trait, you may get high immediately by paying 2 supplies instead of one.\nStrong: Gain 2 fortunes when high and 2 Misfortunes when not.\nHomemade: Your drug doesn\u2019t cost supply, when used roll Create, on failure lose Hp equal to your {vitality d6}. Regardless, you are high.",p="Flip a coin, on Heads gain Fortune on Tails gain Misfortune.\nSupply: when you fail a check in a round, spend a supply and roll 2d6. On a 7 you succeed, otherwise gain nothing.",o="You gain Misfortune. The next time one of your allies would gain Misfortune, they instead gain nothing. Your goodwill lasts until it is used, and you may have any number of stacks. You may not use goodwill on another Giving trait.\nSupply: when an ally would be attacked or suffer an ill effect, spend a supply and become the target instead.",n="Your keepsake is an object that is always on your person. Whenever you fail a Dex Defense, you drop your keepsake in an adjacent space, and you must spend your item interaction to pick it up. If your keepsake is destroyed or lost, after the situation you may repair or remake your keepsake using 1 supply, or 1 scrap using a successful create check.\nIf your keepsake wasn\u2019t destroyed or lost and is still on your person, gain fortune. Otherwise, gain Misfortune.",m="Did you really follow the plan? Gain fortune if you did and misfortune otherwise.\nSupply: You plan a way you could use a supply as a note. You may give that note to a player in a scene that you aren't in by using a supply, and that character gets that supply and must read your note out.",l="Gain Fortune, the next time one of your allies would gain fortune, they instead do not and get nothing. This fortune debt lasts until it's paid, and the party may owe multiple fortunes. You may not pay the Fortune debt using another Self Interested Trait. Giving and Self Interest do not cancel each other.",k=t.jY
return A.b([A.fw(A.b([A.fe("You were so tired. You just needed to let go. The character must ignore an obligation or problem. Until the arc is resolved, the first time you fail a defense in each situation, if you are high, the high ends. If you weren\u2019t high, you gain hurting, the next time you get high you instead do not and lose hurting. If you end the situation without losing this high gain a wound.","comp_addict_hurten","Hurten"),A.fe("There are things you want to do, and things you need. Sometimes that means giving up something. Until the arc is resolved, choose a skill you are proficient in, Downgrade your dice with that skill by 1.","comp_addict_broke","Broke")],k),q,q,"epic_addict","trait_addict","Addict"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("In the face of fire you doubled down and have come up burned. Adventuring: When you fail a skill to deal with a problem, you must fully deal with the problem and all side problems before dealing with anything else, all unrelated checks have disadvantage until you do. In Combat: The first time you miss an attack in each situation, DM picks 1 of the targets, you have disadvantage on all attacks that don\u2019t include that enemy as a target, until you kill them.","comp_confidence_double_down","Double Down"),A.fe("You didn\u2019t respect your limits and others took glee in seeing you down a peg. Until you fail a check during a situation, all Convince and Conceal checks you make have a -1 to success. This also applies to any skill attempting to alter a person\u2019s opinion of you.","comp_confidence_overconfident","Overconfident")],k),"If you acted with confidence, gain fortune. Otherwise, gain misfortune.\nSupply: Pick a skill, you gain +1 to success with that skill until you fail.","If you succeeded on your first check in the situation, gain fortune. Otherwise, gain misfortune.\nSupply: gain a +1 to attacks until you miss an attack.","epic_confidence","trait_confidence","Confidence"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("Combat when you start your turn not concentrating on something, you have disadvantage on all checks that target allies. Adventuring, once you have started a problem you ignore allies until you have finished it.","comp_distractible_not_listening","Sorry I Wasn\u2019t Listening"),A.fe("you tried to do many things and half did all of them. Combat, when you use an ability that you can concentrate on, you must concentrate on it, even if you are already concentrating. If you finish your turn without using an ability that requires concentration, end what you are concentrating on.","comp_distractible_multitasker","Multitasker")],k),"If you got distracted or engaged in an unnecessary task, gain fortune, otherwise gain misfortune. You must have an ability that requires concentration to take Distractible.","If you spent most of your turns concentrating or failed {Level / 3} concentration checks gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.\nSupply: You may reroll concentration checks by paying 1 supply.","epic_distractible","trait_distractible","Distractible"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("Oh you did have plans, that's what you were forgetting. Adventuring, you have -1 to Convince results with people you have a relationship with. Combat: You have -1 to checks to help allies.","comp_forgetful_eta","ETA?"),A.fe("You did have plans. Adventuring, you have a +1 to all project rolls. Combat: you have a -1 on any check against a target you targeted last round.","comp_forgetful_i_forgot","Oh Yea, I Forgot")],k),"If you forget something gain fortune otherwise gain misfortune.\nSupply: if you forget to use your supply in a situation, you gain 1 extra supply next situation.","If you didn't use your [action], or [Reaction] on at least {Level / 4} turns, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.\nSupply: if you forget to use your supply in a situation, you gain 1 extra supply next story.","epic_forgetful","trait_forgetful","Forgetful"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("But what if you make it? Adventuring: When you fail a check, reroll the check with disadvantage. On Failure, also lose 1 cash. Combat: When you fail a check using your action, reroll with disadvantage. On Failure, also lose 1 cash.","comp_gambler_double_or_nothing","Double or Nothing"),A.fe("You just can\u2019t stop yourself. Combat: When you succeed using your action, you have a -1 to result on your next action. Adventuring: When you succeed a check, you have a -1 to the result of your next check.","comp_gambler_the_rush","The Rush")],k),p,p,"epic_gambler","trait_gambler","Gambler"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("Adventure: when someone asks for help and you haven\u2019t acted you must help them. Combat: once per ally per situation when you start or first become adjacent to an ally, you must spend your action to help them.","comp_giving_cant_say_no","Can\u2019t Say No"),A.fe("Adventuring: once per ally per situation, if they have a wound, make a d6 check. On success, they heal a wound and you suffer a wound. On problems, suffer a wound. Combat: once per ally per situation when you start or become adjacent to an ally who isn\u2019t full health, roll {Half vitality d6}. They heal that much and you take double that amount.","comp_giving_more_than_you_can_give","More Than You Can Give")],k),o,o,"epic_giving","trait_giving","Giving"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("Combat: the first time an ally within 4 takes damage each round, give them resistance to the damage, and you take the full damage from the attack. Adventuring: the First time an ally would make a defense, they gain advantage on the check and you take 1 adventuring damage.","comp_helpful_ill_handle_it","I\u2019ll Handle It"),A.fe("Combat: the first time any ally within 4 would make a skill check, you dash adjacent to them and they make the check with disadvantage. Adventuring: The first time an ally tries to make a Brute, Finesse, or Create check, they make it with disadvantage.","comp_helpful_in_the_way","In the Way")],k),"If you targeted an ally with an ability or aided them in a skill, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.\nSupply: when an ally would make a check, spend a supply and give them advantage on the check.","If you targeted an ally with an ability or aided them in a skill at least {Level / 3} times, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.\nSupply: when an ally would make a check, spend a supply and give them advantage on the check.","epic_helpful","trait_helpful","Helpful"),A.fw(B.d5,"If the situation was caused by following your plan Gain Misfortune, otherwise Gain Fortune.","If you died, or placed yourself in risky situations, gain fortune. Otherwise, gain misfortune.\nSupply: On your first combat turn of a situation, spend a supply and gain +3 speed this turn.","epic_impulsive","trait_impulsive","Impulsive"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("Adventuring: Your keepsake causes you and allies in your presence to have -1 to convince checks. Combat: You and allies within 4 of your keepsake have -1 to concentration checks.","comp_keepsake_it_stinks","It Stinks"),A.fe("Adventuring: you must also drop your keepsake when you make a Str or Dex defense. Combat: When you drop your keepsake, make a concentration check. On Problems, your keepsake is damaged and you don\u2019t gain its effects until you can rest, or repair it with a create check and a scrap.","comp_keepsake_falling_apart","It\u2019s Falling Apart")],k),n,n,"epic_keepsake","trait_keepsake","Keepsake"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("You only count as having a plan if you have a list of objectives and steps.","comp_planner_the_list","The List"),A.fe("You only count as having a plan if you have discussed the plan with all of the involved characters and they agree to the plan.","comp_planner_open_to_feedback","Open to Feedback")],k),m,m,"epic_planner","trait_planner","Planner"),A.fw(B.d5,"If you had to do anything dangerous gain misfortune. Otherwise gain fortune.","If you lost half your health or died you gain misfortune. Otherwise gain fortune.","epic_nervous","trait_nervous","Nervous"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("You never stick to your plan, instead overreacting to the situation. Adventuring: You have -1 to checks related to the primary situation or plan. Combat: You have a -1 to all checks related to Objectives.","comp_reactive_but_you_said","But You Said You Would"),A.fe("You just keep waiting for the right opportunity. Adventuring, if you are the first person to try to deal with a problem you have disadvantage. Combat: If you are the first person to target that character, you have disadvantage on the check.","comp_reactive_timing_is_right","When the Timing Is Right")],k),"If you joined someone else or tagged along, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.","If you undermined the enemy\u2019s plan, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.","epic_reactive","trait_reactive","Reactive"),A.fw(B.d5,"If you didn\u2019t rush or panic, gain fortune otherwise misfortune.","If you didn\u2019t take the [Run], [Retreat], or [Ready] actions gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.","epic_relaxed","trait_relaxed","Relaxed"),A.fw(B.d5,"Pick a skill when you pick this. If you only used that skill in the situation, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.","If you have made any Skill check, gain Fortune, otherwise gain misfortune.","epic_savant","trait_savant","Savant"),A.fw(B.d5,"You regain a supply and gain an exhaustion. Explain what you found and why getting it wore you out.","If you looted or gathered scrap, gain fortune, otherwise gain misfortune.","epic_scrapper","trait_scrapper","Scrapper"),A.fw(B.d5,l,l,"epic_self_interested","trait_self_interested","Self Interested"),A.fw(B.d5,"If you used Convince or failed a Cha defense, Gain misfortune, otherwise gain Fortune.","If no enemy got adjacent to you, gain Fortune, otherwise gain Misfortune.","epic_shy","trait_shy","Shy"),A.fw(B.d5,"If you used convince, Gain Fortune. Otherwise gain Misfortune.","If you ended your turn adjacent to an ally at least {Level / 3} times, gain Fortune, otherwise gain Misfortune.","epic_social","trait_social","Social"),A.fw(B.d5,"If it was a dangerous situation, even for you, gain Fortune. Otherwise Gain Misfortune.","If you were attacked at least {Level / 3} times, Gain Fortune, otherwise gain Misfortune.","epic_thrill_seeker","trait_thrill_seeker","Reckless"),A.fw(B.d5,"gain a misfortune and the first 2 times you would use supply in this situation you do not use supply.","If you spent your object interaction tinkering at least {Level/3} times, gain Fortune, otherwise gain Misfortune.","epic_tinkerer","trait_tinkerer","Tinkerer"),A.fw(A.b([A.fe("why can\u2019t they just do it. Adventuring: The first time an ally with you rolls problems make an attack against them, on success deal 1 hit. Combat: The first time an ally within in range of one of your attack fails a check, make roll an attack against them. On Success, deal {Level d6} ignoring resistance and shield.","comp_violent_temper","Temper"),A.fe("Why can\u2019t i do anything right. Adventuring: Whenever you roll problems on a proficient skill, attack yourself and deal 1 hit on success. Combat: Once each turn, when you fail an attack, roll an attack against yourself, and deal {Level d6} damage on a success ignoring resistance and shield.","comp_violent_frustration","Frustration")],k),"If you made an attack against someone, gain fortune otherwise gain Misfortune.","If most of your actions were attacks or caused damage, gain fortune. Otherwise gain misfortune.","epic_violent","trait_violent","Violent")],A.ao("C<h7>"))})
